From a0a53bbd3021f4fb06e23dd55b64dc9e5af8cf85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:13:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] macro_rules: brackets and braces in generic arguments are
 skimmed as token trees

symphonia-core 0.6.1 src/dsp/fft/no_simd.rs:38 (port mp3rgain),
a lazy_static item `static ref $N:ident : $T:ty = $e:expr;` given
`Box<[Complex<f32>; (1 << $bi) >> 1]>`:

    MACRO<..fft_twiddle_table> BUG: src/macro_rules/eval.cpp: TODO:
    Macro_InvokeRules_MatchPattern - No arm matched - (18, 29), (0, 81),
    (0, 81), (0, 81)

Reference, Paths > GenericArgs: a GenericArg is a Type, a
GenericArgsConst (a BlockExpression, a literal or a path) or a binding;
an ArrayType's length is an Expression. Inside the `[..]` of an array
or slice type and the `{..}` of a const argument, `<`, `>`, `<<` and
`>>` are operators, not angle brackets.

consume_tt_angle, which every `ty` / `path` / `expr` skimmer uses to
find the `>` closing generic arguments (consume_path in type and
expression mode, consume_type_TraitList through it, turbofish method
calls), took a parenthesised group as one token tree but walked
`[..]` and `{..}` token by token. The `>>` in the array length closed
`Box<` (its first half pushed back as the `>`), the `ty` fragment ended
inside the brackets and the arm wanted `=`. Brackets and braces are
now consumed as token trees like parentheses.

The real parser was not affected: it parses the length as an expression.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---

diff --git a/src/macro_rules/eval.cpp b/src/macro_rules/eval.cpp
index ef9ca9d0..6350fc58 100644
--- a/src/macro_rules/eval.cpp
+++ b/src/macro_rules/eval.cpp
@@ -1077,8 +1077,8 @@ namespace
             {
             }
 
-            // Consume TTs separately
-            if( lex.next() == TOK_PAREN_OPEN )
+            // Delimited groups are single TTs: a `<`/`>`/`<<`/`>>` inside an array length or a const block is an operator
+            if( lex.next() == TOK_PAREN_OPEN || lex.next() == TOK_SQUARE_OPEN || lex.next() == TOK_BRACE_OPEN )
             {
                 consume_tt(lex);
             }
diff --git a/src/version.cpp b/src/version.cpp
index 03e3a878..ed5954fa 100644
--- a/src/version.cpp
+++ b/src/version.cpp
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 #define VERSION_PATCH   0
 
 // Number of the last patch in this fork's series: every fix commit bumps it
-#define VERSION_SERIES  472
+#define VERSION_SERIES  473
 // rlibs written by an older series are refused (0 = accept all)
 #define VERSION_SERIES_FLOOR    0
 
